# Performance constraints (social addon)

## Non-negotiables

- UI closed → effectively idle (events only)
- No permanent `OnUpdate` for business logic
- In combat: no full-list rebuild storms
- Prefer ≪ 1 MB SavedVariables

## Budget

| Phase | Expectation |
|-------|-------------|
| UI closed | Events only |
| UI open | Interaction + ≤10 Hz dirty coalesce |
| In combat | No permanent OnUpdate |
| Login sync | Bursty then quiet |

Bar: invisible next to WA/Details/nameplates.

## Do / don’t

| Do | Don’t |
|----|-------|
| Event-driven roster / Core apply | Per-frame proximity / combat scans |
| Dirty-flag UI; refresh ≤10 Hz when open | Rebuild full lists per BeefNet message |
| Cap **lossy UI caches** only | Delete or expire Church records (Law 7) |
| Cache roster lookups | Full guild rescan every refresh |
| `C_Timer` when a one-shot delay is required | Permanent `OnUpdate` for net or Core |

```lua
-- ✅ GOOD — disable when idle
frame:SetScript("OnUpdate", nil)

-- ❌ BAD — net parse or Core mutate every frame
frame:SetScript("OnUpdate", function(_, elapsed) end)
```

## Cross-cutting throttle

- BeefNet: CTL pacing; inbound rate limits; reply suppression — see ceremony-runtime / BeefNet keepers (not archived `beefnet-messaging.mdc`)
- No permanent tickers for business logic

## SV size

Prefer ≪ 1 MB. Church records are never deleted. Cap lossy UI caches only — not the store, Chronicle, or Gora records.
